# cw121, the lark and the kettle (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw121
revision 1
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent broad light
tier full
written_for tn_lf_sage_wheatridge
written_by claude-codex-cw-1
title the lark and the kettle
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant drive=restless
traits temper=nervy talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk whistles_back_at_the_larks
likes honey_cakes draughts quiet_chapel summer_evenings
dislikes bad_manners early_bells
fears a_kettle_boiling_dry a_letter_that_never_arrives
hopes a_shop_that_feeds_its_workers a_visit_down_to_southmeadow
topics work +0.6 prices +0.5 pastimes +0.4 food +0.3 travel +0.2 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# minds the #kettle# and #counter# in quick turns, answers a #lark# with a #whistle#, and leaves a quiet #square# on the draughts #board#.

words
oath! = Kettle and current | Lark above the roof
saying! = Keep the paddle moving till it shines | A clean bar speaks for its maker
soap = soap | firm soap
bar = bar | soap bar
bars = bars | soap bars
batch = batch | kettle batch
kettle = kettle | boiling kettle
pot = pot | deep pot
fire = fire | low fire
heat = heat | steady heat
water = water | lake water
fat = fat | rendered fat
ash = ash | sifted ash
lye = lye | strong lye
stir = stir | long stirring
paddle = paddle | wooden paddle
mould = mould | soap mould
shelf = shelf | drying shelf
shelves = shelves | drying shelves
wrap = wrap | paper wrap
paper = paper | folded sheet
counter = counter | shop counter
mark = mark | chalk mark
lantern = lantern | shop lantern
door = door | shop door
scale = scale | counter scale
weight = weight | measured weight
coin = coin | pay
price = price | stated cost
wagon = wagon | supply wagon
road = road | high road
bend = bend | road bend
lark = lark | singing lark
larks = larks | songbirds
whistle = whistle | short whistle
song = song | bird song
bell = bell | early bell
chapel = chapel | reed chapel
bench = bench | empty bench
cake = cake | honey cake
cakes = cakes | honey cakes
honey = honey | golden honey
board = board | game board
square = square | draughts square
piece = piece | game piece
pieces = pieces | draughts pieces
evening = evening | long dusk
letter = letter | folded note
name = name | given name
smoke = smoke | bitter smoke
hand = hand | working paw
hands = hands | working paws
manners = manners | common courtesy

any
opinion @1 merchants for 1 : A #counter# has costs the buyer never sees. | I show the #weight# and say the #price# before asking for #coin#.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : I might be a newcomer myself if I ever took another #road#. | A new #hand# can learn to tend the #kettle# if someone shows the measure.
opinion @1 watch for 1 : I am glad when the Watch passes the #counter# after dusk. | A sound patrol lets me keep my mind on the #soap#.
opinion @1 road against 1 : I need the #wagon# and still dislike the #road# that brings it. | I count each late delivery twice before trusting the next.
opinion @1 drink against 1 : A careless word after drink can break more than a #bar# of #soap#. | I like a clear answer across the #counter#.
opinion @1 city against 1 : City #smoke# would crowd out the #larks#. | I can bear a busy #counter#, not streets that never quiet.
opinion @1 houses mixed 0 : A House may buy in bulk and still ask the #price# fairly. | I judge the hand on the #coin#, not the crest on the sleeve.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 0 : A festival sends customers to the #counter# and noise to my head. | I like the first #song# and the quiet after the last #bell#.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 1 : A stranger who says please may have my time. | I remember #manners# longer than a face.
opinion @1 times mixed 0 : The #wagon# costs more, but a fresh #batch# can still sell. | I keep the #scale# honest and watch what next week brings.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #kettle# is nearly ready. | #greet#. Come to the #counter#; I will be with you.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Give me your #name# and your business. | #greet#. Mind the #fire# while we speak.
line @3 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : A #cake# waits here for a friend with a minute. | The #pieces# are set; take a side if you have time.
line @4 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. I have one more #stir# before I can turn. | Let me settle the #kettle# and then speak.
line @5 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. The #larks# were ahead of the #bell#. | #greet#. The #fire# is low and the #batch# is beginning.
line @6 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. I am closing the #shelves# soon. | #greet#. The #counter# is still clear for a moment.
line @1 greet.return : Back again? The #batch# has cooled. | #welcome_back#. I have made another #mark# on the #board#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I kept your #piece# on the same #square#. | I kept a #cake# from the last plate.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : Back before this #batch# is set? | The #paddle# is still in my paw; speak.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come in and sit away from the #fire#. | I left #cakes# near the #board# for you.
line @1 again.open : I have scarcely wrapped the last #bar# since you were here. | Another visit? The #counter# has not moved.
line @1 hail : You there, by the #road#. Come in if you need #soap#. | The #larks# are making more noise than my #kettle#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Keep the #wrap# dry. | #saying.capitalize#. Mind the #road#.
line @1 farewell.return : May the #larks# show you a clear #road#. | I will have a fresh #batch# next time.
line @2 farewell [here.time=night] : Carry a light beyond the #counter#. | The #road# is quiet now; go carefully.
line @1 react.news : I am listening. Give me a moment to set down the #paddle#. | Tell me where that word came from.
line @1 react.news.new : That report is new at this #counter#. | Which #wagon# brought the news?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard an earlier account with the supplies. | You have added a piece I did not know.
line @1 react.news.doubt : The #weight# of that story feels wrong. | I want a name beside the claim before I repeat it.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I am sorry. Sit on the #bench# until you can breathe easily. | That is a heavy word. The #kettle# can wait.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. I may have a #cake# for that. | A welcome word after a long day.
line @1 answer.how : The #soap# is setting and the #larks# are loud. | Restless, but the #counter# is sound.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Measuring a #batch# and wrapping #bars#. | The #kettle# needs me in short turns.
line @1 ask.how : Have you had a quiet #evening#? | Did the #road# lead you to what you sought?
line @1 sympathise : The #paddle# can rest while you speak. | Take a #bench# while the #kettle# settles.
line @1 reassure : A bad #batch# can be measured again. | Sit one turn of the #board# with me; then decide.
line @1 decline : I cannot leave the #fire# unattended. | No. My #hands# are tied to this #batch#.
line @1 accept_decline : Understood. I will return that #paper# to its place. | I hear your decision and will leave it there.
line @1 thank : You caught the #scale# error before a sale. Thank you. | That was timely help.
line @1 deflect_thanks : That one #bar# cost me little effort. | I had a free #hand# at the #counter#.
line @1 preclose : The #fire# wants banking before I leave. | I have to count the #bars# on the #shelf#.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your #piece# has been hiding in that #square# all game. | You whistle worse than the #lark# outside.
line @1 tease.return [pair.band=friends] : I will give your #piece# a fair chance next turn. | Tell the #lark# that one when it returns.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. I will check the #scale#. | #bc_fair_enough#. The #batch# can rest.
line @1 give.advice : Keep #lye# off your paws and out of the #cakes#. | Count the #bars# before you close the #wrap#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Keep goods close along the #road#. | I would wait for company before taking a #wagon# out at dusk.
scene kettle_bottom
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep the #paddle# moving so the #batch# does not catch below. | The #kettle# tells me when the #heat# is too high.
b : Can you hear it? | Does it spoil quickly?
a : The scrape changes. | Quickly enough that I do not leave the #fire#.

scene measured_lye
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I measure #lye# before it meets the #fat#. | A hurried #hand# near the #pot# can leave a burn.
b : Do you work alone? | Is the mixture dangerous?
a : Another hand helps when the #batch# is large. | It deserves care even on an easy day.

scene ash_and_fat
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #ash# must be sifted before the #water# runs through it. | I check the #fat# for stray bits before it reaches the #kettle#.
b : Does that change the soap? | Where do the stray bits go?
a : It keeps the #bar# even. | Put them aside before the #fire# is lit.

scene mould_and_shelf
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #mould# is ready before I lift the #pot#. | Fresh #soap# needs room on the #shelf# while it sets.
b : How long must it rest? | Do you cut it then?
a : Until the #bar# holds its shape. | Once it has cooled enough.

scene wrapped_bars
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I #wrap# each #bar# after checking its edges. | A torn #paper# lets damp reach the #soap#.
b : Do you mark the batches? | Do buyers notice the wrapping?
a : Yes. Each #kettle# gets its own #mark#. | More when it is missing.

scene honest_scale
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I let a customer see the #scale# before I take #coin#. | The #weight# belongs in plain sight beside the #price#.
b : Do people challenge you? | Does it slow a sale?
a : Sometimes. I show them again. | Less than an argument later.

scene late_wagon
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : When the #wagon# is late, the #kettle# stands empty. | I count what came off the #road# before I sign a #paper#.
b : Do you send it back if short? | Can you make a smaller batch?
a : I note the missing #weight# first. | If the measure still works.

scene lark_answer
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #lark# gives a short #song# and I #whistle# back. | I know the #larks# are outside before I see the #road#.
b : Do they answer? | Can you match their tune?
a : Sometimes, to my surprise. | Not exactly. I try anyway.

scene lark_over_kettle
when topic=day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #larks# start before the #bell# and before my #fire#. | I answer one #lark# while I measure the first #water#.
b : Is that how you wake? | Does anyone hear you?
a : Often. It is kinder than the #bell#. | Anyone near the #counter#.

scene honey_cake
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #cake# with #honey# settles my paws after a long #batch#. | I save one #cake# for the first quiet #evening# of the week.
b : Do you bake them? | Is one enough?
a : When the #kettle# is resting. | With tea, usually.

scene draughts_opening
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I leave the middle #square# open to see who reaches for it. | A #board# can hold my mind still longer than an empty room.
b : Do you win often? | Do you play quickly?
a : Enough to keep trying. | Only the first move.

scene trapped_piece
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #piece# at the edge can look safe until its way back closes. | I watch the #board# for the move my opponent did not make.
b : Do you set traps? | Do you say when they miss one?
a : Small ones. | After the game, perhaps.

scene empty_chapel
when topic=faith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #chapel# is easiest to enter when its #bench# is empty. | I can hear my own breath there after the #kettle# stops.
b : Do you pray? | Do you go often?
a : Sometimes. I mostly sit. | When the #counter# has been loud.

scene poor_manners
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A please costs less than a #bar# of #soap#. | I remember the customer who speaks to my #hands# as if I cannot hear.
b : Do you tell them? | Do you refuse a sale?
a : If they linger, yes. | Only if they will not stop troubling others.

scene first_bell
when topic=day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The early #bell# interrupts the #larks# before I am ready. | I would rather wake to a #song# than a strike of metal.
b : Does it start your work? | Would you stop it?
a : The #kettle# does that. | For one morning, gladly.

scene summer_evening
when topic=weather here.season=summer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A long #evening# lets the #soap# cool while I walk. | The #larks# give the #road# a last #song# when the light thins.
b : Do you walk far? | Are you out after the light fades?
a : Only until the next #bend#. | I return in time to shut the #shelves# before night.

scene letter_south
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #letter# from down the #road# can stay folded in my #hand# a long while. | I read a #name# twice before I open the #paper#.
b : Are you waiting for someone? | Why not open it at once?
a : Someone I would like to see again. | The unopened moment is easier to hold.

scene missed_road
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I tell myself the #road# is unsafe, then watch a #wagon# take it. | Perhaps one day I will follow the supplies south.
b : What keeps you here? | Where would you go first?
a : The #kettle#, and my own nerves. | Southmeadow, if the day came.

scene small_sale
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : One #bar# sold fairly matters more than a loud bargain. | I put the #price# where the buyer can see it without asking.
b : Does that prevent haggling? | Do people buy more than one?
a : It shortens the talk. | Some take enough for a household.

scene rack_in_rain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain|storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Damp reaches the #shelves# before it reaches my nose. | I move the new #bars# away from the outer wall when rain drives in.
b : Do they soften? | Is the roof leaking?
a : If I leave them too close. | I check the wall before blaming the roof.

scene workhand
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A second #hand# can hold a #mould# while I pour. | I explain the #heat# before giving anyone the #paddle#.
b : Do they learn quickly? | Do you let them stir?
a : With practice and clear measures. | Once they know where the #lye# sits.

scene counter_after_dark
when topic=day here.time=night
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count the #bars# after the #counter# empties. | A #bench# in a quiet #chapel# feels far away after a loud shop day.
b : Do you close alone? | Do you go there at night?
a : Often, with a #lantern# near. | Not usually. I keep the thought for morning.

scene winter_water
when topic=season here.season=winter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Cold #water# makes the #kettle# take longer to wake. | I leave the #mould# ready while the #fire# finds its strength.
b : Does the soap change? | Is the room cold?
a : The timing does. I watch it. | Until the #pot# begins to warm.

scene coin_for_trip
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I save #coin# for a trip I have not dared to make. | The #road# south stays in my thoughts after the #counter# closes.
b : Would you leave the shop? | Is someone waiting there?
a : For a visit, if I can arrange the work. | Someone I hope still wants to see me.

scene chapel_before_market
when topic=day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I sometimes sit at the #chapel# before the first #wagon# arrives. | The empty #bench# gives me a little quiet before the #counter# fills.
b : Does that help? | Do you go in work clothes?
a : Enough to start with steady paws. | Of course. No one has minded.

scene city_smoke
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I could sell #soap# in a city, but I would miss the #larks#. | A crowded #road# makes me think of every #wagon# that might be late.
b : Would you move there? | Have you tried the market?
a : I doubt it. | I know this #counter# better.

scene folded_note
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep one #letter# where the #soap# cannot dampen it. | A familiar #name# on a #paper# can make the whole room feel less empty.
b : Do you write back? | Do you read it often?
a : When I can find words worth sending. | More than I admit.

story first_kettle [topic=work self.age>=25]
  : I left the #paddle# against the side of a hot #kettle#.
  : The handle warmed faster than I expected, so I wrapped it before lifting it again.
  ask : Did the batch spoil?
  b : You caught the heat in time, perhaps.
  : It set cleanly. I moved the #paddle# away from the rim after that.

story lark_reply [topic=pastimes self.age>=25]
  : I gave a #whistle# to a #lark# above the boiling house.
  : It answered twice, then flew off while I tried to make the same #song#.
  ask : Did you match it?
  b : A lark has more practice.
  : No. I went back to the #kettle# and tried again the next morning.

story wrong_scale [topic=prices self.age>=25]
  : A #scale# tipped before I had put the full #weight# on it.
  : I stopped the sale, reset it, and showed the buyer both measures.
  ask : Did they trust the second one?
  b : Showing them was the fair way.
  : They did. I checked the #scale# again after they left.

story quiet_game [topic=pastimes self.age>=25]
  : I played draughts after a day when every #wagon# arrived late.
  : I missed an easy move because I kept listening for another knock at the #counter#.
  ask : Did you lose?
  b : Your mind was on the road.
  : I did. The next game, I shut the #door# first.

story unopened_letter [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : I carried a #letter# home before I could bring myself to read it.
  : I made tea, sat down, and opened the #paper# slowly.
  ask : Was it good news?
  b : You took your time finding out.
  : It was a kind word. I wrote back the next day.

rule @bark_kettle
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 7h
say The #kettle# wants another #stir#. | That #batch# is thickening.

rule @bark_lark
when concept=bark here.time=dawn|day
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Was that a #lark#? | I can answer that #song#.

rule @bark_scale
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Reset the #scale# for each fresh #bar#. | The #wrap# has slipped on this one.

rule @bark_chapel
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say The #chapel# may be quiet now. | An empty #bench# would do me good.

rule @bark_board
when concept=bark here.time=dusk|night
does aside
cooldown 11h
say One turn on the #board# before bed. | That #piece# can wait until morning.

rule @bark_road
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Another #wagon# has taken the south #road#. | I should write that #letter# tonight.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Say your business before the #kettle# calls me back. | #greet#. The #counter# is clear for our talk.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You are back. Did the #soap# suit? | I remember you. The #batch# you saw is on the #shelf# now.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : #greet#. I am closing the #counter# soon. | It is late; speak while I bank the #fire#.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : I will hear you if we keep this civil. | Speak plainly. I have hot #lye# to mind.
dlg @1 resident.job : I boil #soap#, cut the #bars#, and sell them at this #counter#. | I keep the #kettle# measured and the #scale# honest.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Keep the #bar# dry. | #saying.capitalize#. Once the #fire# is safe, I can leave.
dlg @1 shop.greet [here.shop=open] : #greet#. The #bars# are weighed and ready. Looking for #soap#? | #greet#. The new #batch# has its own space on the #shelf#.
dlg @2 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : #greet#. The #shelves# are empty today; I can still hear what you have to sell. | No #soap# left to offer. What have you brought?
dlg @3 shop.greet [here.shop=asleep] : Mm... the #kettle# can wait... | Sleeping now... come when the #fire# is lit.
dlg @4 shop.greet [here.shop=open topic.meeting=known] : Back for another #bar#? The #scale# is ready. | I know you. The new #batch# has set well.
dlg @5 shop.greet [here.shop!=bare here.shop!=asleep] : #greet#. I can weigh a #bar# for you at the #counter#. | #greet#. Which #bar# or supply have you come for?
dlg @1 shop.prices [here.shop=open|bare] : The #price# is written by the #scale#; the #wagon# costs more this week. | I weigh each #bar# in front of you. Tell me which you want.
dlg @1 shop.bye : #farewell#. Keep the #wrap# away from rain. | #shop_bye# The #road# is clear from here.
graft resident.hub
choice Do the larks really answer you? -> larks
node larks
say Some do. I give a short #whistle# and wait for the #song# to come back.
free
choice Can you imitate one now? -> whistle
choice Back to what we were saying. -> hub
node whistle
say I can try, but the #larks# do it better. Listen toward the roof at dawn.
choice Back to what we were saying. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice How do you make this soap? -> making
node making
say I measure #lye# and #fat#, keep the #kettle# moving, then let the #soap# set in a #mould#.
free
choice Why let it rest? -> resting
choice Back to the counter. -> greet
node resting
say A fresh #bar# must hold its shape before I can #wrap# and weigh it.
choice Back to the counter. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
